<title>CANADA: Canada M1 money supply falls in January.</title>
<headline>Canada M1 money supply falls in January.</headline>
<dateline>OTTAWA 1997-02-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Canadian M1 money supply fell by C$1.21 billion to C$68.53 billion in January from C$69.74 billion in December, the Bank of Canada said on Friday.</p>
<p>					   Jan 97     Dec 96     Jan 96</p>
<p>M1					  68.53	69.74	59.28</p>
<p>M2					 395.28     398.32     388.67</p>
<p>M3					 498.28     500.53     472.55</p>
<p>Note - Figures are unadjusted, in billions of dollars.  </p>
<p>   Chartered bank assets			 Jan	   Dec</p>
<p>   Net foreign currency			-16.27	-13.93</p>
<p>   Canadian dollar			     685.02	685.04</p>
<p>   Total Canadian liquid assets	    105.33	108.04</p>
<p>				    Wk to Feb 19  Chg on wk  Chg on yr</p>
<p>Notes in circulation		  26.536  -0.167     +0.648</p>
<p>Government cash balances	     6.795  +0.523     -0.073</p>
<p>Govt securities outstanding	461.911  +1.456     +5.208</p>
<p>Treasury bills			 128.900  -0.800    -30.500</p>
<p>Canada savings bonds		  33.127  -0.044     +2.106</p>
<p>All figures in billions of dollars.</p>
<p>((Reuters Ottawa Bureau 613-235-6745))</p>
</text>
